{
  "schema_version": "pals.request-grammar.v1",
  "notes": "Closed vocabulary for turning a learner request into one Lean proposition without a model. A request is accepted only if every character is consumed by an entry below; anything else is a miss and the request keeps its existing route. To widen the grammar, add rows here (a function, a property, a domain, a filler word); no code change is needed for a new function or property that fits the templates. Forms are Python regular expressions applied to the normalized text (superscript digits are written as ^k, NFKC applied, lower-cased). The named group v is the variable letter; k and other slot groups are the parameters of the function. search_terms are the deterministic Recipe-search query words of a function or property. A property may name preferred_method: among Recipes that bind, those with that proof_method_tag are tried first. Output-language instructions (filler_patterns) draw on a closed set of words so that free text cannot ride along. Domain 'patterns' and 'filler_patterns' are regular expressions on the normalized text; 'forms' are literals (normalized when the table is built). A function binder may name the function symbol (group fn): standalone occurrences of that letter are then consumed too. Widening notes: slot kind 'decimal' is 0|[1-9]\\d{0,8} with an optional .\\d{1,6} fraction; a form may override the function's lean_body; a form with name_only is a bare function name (e.g. 'the fourth power function'): it is consumed only beside a formula of the same function whose body agrees, and it is a request on its own only when 'alone' is not false. Two different functions may overlap only by containment (the longer match wins); any other overlap is ambiguous and a miss. Variables are the real-variable letters s t u v w x y; e (Euler), n k m (integers), z (complex) and capital letters never match. Properties are listed with uniformly_continuous before continuous, so 'uniformly continuous' is never read as 'continuous'; plain 単調増加 / monotone increasing / increasing / one-to-one / 1対1 are not rows because they are ambiguous. Not in the table on purpose (add a row to widen): a minus sign in a x - b, a coefficient with a power c x^k, unapplied or name-only functions other than the squaring function. hypothetical: a property followed by 'とする'/'でも' (after_property) or a formula right after '設/令/let' (before_formula) is an assumption, not a request, and is a miss. In domain patterns {v} stands for the request's own variable letter, so 'for all t' with a formula in x is a miss. The bare words 定义/定義 are not fillers (a question about the definition of continuity is not a request to prove it); only 'the term, then 定义' (由 f(x)=x^3 定义) is consumed, by a filler pattern that starts at the consumed term (the NUL character stands for it).",
